{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0037","statement":"Tweet2vec is a character composition model that finds vector-space representations of whole tweets by learning complex, non-local dependencies in character sequences.","source_span":"We propose a character composition model, tweet2vec, which finds vector-space representations of whole tweets by learning complex, non-local dependencies in character sequences."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0037","statement":"The tweet2vec encoder is publicly available.","source_span":"Our tweet2vec encoder is publicly available."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0037","statement":"The training dataset consisted of 2 million tweets with about 0.92 million unique word types.","source_span":"In our moderately sized training dataset of 2 million tweets, there were about 0.92 million unique word types."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0037","statement":"The proposed model is a Bi-directional Gated Recurrent Unit (Bi-GRU) neural network for learning tweet representations.","source_span":"We propose a Bi-directional Gated Recurrent Unit (Bi-GRU) BIBREF5 neural network for learning tweet representations."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0037","statement":"The training objective is to maximize cross-entropy loss for predicting hashtags for a post from its latent representation.","source_span":"we formulate our training objective to maximize cross-entropy loss at the task of predicting hashtags for a post from its latent representation."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0037","statement":"The model treats white-space as a special character during its forward and backward pass over the sequence.","source_span":"Treating white-space as a special character itself, the model does a forward and backward pass over the entire sequence"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0037","statement":"BIBREF2 present a bidirectional LSTM for composing word vectors from their constituent characters.","source_span":"BIBREF2 challenge this assumption and present a bidirectional Long Short Term Memory (LSTM) BIBREF3 for composing word vectors from their constituent characters"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0037","fact_refs":[0],"question":"What is tweet2vec and what kind of representation does it learn?","answer":"Tweet2vec is a character composition model that learns vector-space representations of whole tweets by capturing complex, non-local dependencies in character sequences."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0037","fact_refs":[2],"question":"How many tweets were in tweet2vec's training dataset, and how many unique word types did it contain?","answer":"The training dataset had 2 million tweets, containing about 0.92 million unique word types."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0037","fact_refs":[3],"question":"What neural network architecture does tweet2vec use to learn tweet representations?","answer":"A Bi-directional Gated Recurrent Unit (Bi-GRU) neural network."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0037","fact_refs":[4],"question":"What is the training objective used to learn tweet2vec's representations?","answer":"The training objective is to maximize cross-entropy loss at the task of predicting hashtags for a post from its latent representation."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0037","fact_refs":[1],"question":"Is the tweet2vec encoder publicly available?","answer":"Yes, the tweet2vec encoder is publicly available."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0037","fact_refs":[5],"question":"How does tweet2vec handle white-space when processing a tweet's characters?","answer":"It treats white-space as a special character itself while doing a forward and backward pass over the entire character sequence."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0038","statement":"The paper introduces the Argus Yes/No Question Answering task, exemplified by the question 'Did Donald Trump announce he is running for president?'","source_span":"As a specific instance, we introduce the Argus Yes/No Question Answering task. The problem is, given a real-world event binary question like Did Donald Trump announce he is running for president?"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0038","statement":"The research is motivated by the Argus automatic reporting system for the Augur prediction market platform.","source_span":"Our research is motivated by the Argus automatic reporting system for the Augur prediction market platform."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0038","statement":"The time domain of dataset questions was restricted from September 1, 2014 to September 1, 2015.","source_span":"the time domain of questions was restricted from September 1, 2014 to September 1, 2015"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0038","statement":"The topic domain of the dataset was focused on politics, sports, and the stock market.","source_span":"topic domain was focused to politics, sports and the stock market"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0038","statement":"Amazon Mechanical Turk users seeded the dataset with an initial, somewhat redundant 250 questions.","source_span":"This seeded the dataset with initial, somewhat redundant 250 questions."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0038","statement":"The dataset was extended with questions autogenerated from 26 templates pertaining to top sporting event winners and US senate or gubernatorial elections.","source_span":"We extended the data with questions autogenerated from 26 templates, pertaining top sporting event winners and US senate or gubernatorial elections."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0038","statement":"The model was also evaluated on the MCTest dataset and the AI2-8grade/CK12 dataset for ranking multiple-choice question answers.","source_span":"We consider the MCTest dataset and the AI2-8grade/CK12 dataset that we introduce below."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0038","statement":"The Syphon preprocessing component of the Argus implementation was used to identify semantic roles of question tokens and produce search keywords for building the evidence dataset.","source_span":"we used the Syphon preprocessing component BIBREF5 of the Argus implementation to identify semantic roles of all question tokens and produce the search keywords"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0038","fact_refs":[0],"question":"What example question illustrates the Argus Yes/No Question Answering task?","answer":"\"Did Donald Trump announce he is running for president?\" — a real-world event binary question that must be answered using retrieved news article fragments as evidence."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0038","fact_refs":[1],"question":"What prediction market platform motivates the Argus research described in the paper?","answer":"The research is motivated by the Argus automatic reporting system for the Augur prediction market platform."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0038","fact_refs":[2,3],"question":"What time period and topics were the Argus dataset's questions restricted to?","answer":"Questions were restricted to the period from September 1, 2014 to September 1, 2015, and to the topics of politics, sports, and the stock market."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0038","fact_refs":[4],"question":"How many initial questions did Amazon Mechanical Turk users contribute to seed the Argus dataset?","answer":"250 initial, somewhat redundant questions."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0038","fact_refs":[5],"question":"How many templates were used to autogenerate additional questions for the Argus dataset, and what did they cover?","answer":"26 templates were used, covering top sporting event winners and US senate or gubernatorial elections."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0038","fact_refs":[6],"question":"Besides the Argus dataset, what other datasets were used to evaluate the multiple-choice question ranking model?","answer":"The MCTest dataset and the AI2-8grade/CK12 dataset."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0039","statement":"The researchers ran a user study with 25 participants to demonstrate the tool's speed and accuracy advantages over conventional methods.","source_span":"We ran a user study with 25 participants, demonstrating that compared to more conventional methods, our tool can increase the speed and the accuracy with which users can track stories about real-world events."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0039","statement":"The researchers manually annotated 7,000 tweets about several different real-world events for assertion detection.","source_span":"We manually annotated $7,000$ tweets about several different real-world events."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0039","statement":"Of the 7,000 annotated tweets, 3,290 (47%) contained assertions.","source_span":"Of the $7,000$ tweets, $3,290$ ( $47\\%$ ) of those tweets containing assertions and the rest containing one of the other speech-acts."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0039","statement":"The supervised Twitter speech-act classifier used to train the assertion detector was developed by Vosoughi et al.","source_span":"trained a state-of-the-art supervised Twitter speech-act classifier, developed by Vosoughi et al. BIBREF3"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0039","statement":"The assertion classifier was evaluated using 20-fold cross validation and achieved an F-score of 0.86.","source_span":"We evaluated the classifier using 20-fold cross validation, with the F-score for classifying assertions being $.86$ ."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0039","statement":"An example boolean query used by the system is 'Boston AND Bombing', which picks out tweets about the 2013 Boston marathon bombings.","source_span":"the query is Boston AND Bombing, which picks out tweets about the 2013 Boston marathon bombings"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0039","statement":"The paper cites the 2011 Japanese earthquake, the 2013 Boston marathon bombings, and the 2015 Paris shootings as examples where Twitter played a major role in disseminating event information.","source_span":"The 2011 Japanese earthquake, the 2013 Boston marathon bombings, and the 2015 Paris shootings are just three examples of an event where Twitter played major role in the dissemination of information."}
